[EXIT STATUS]
.TP
.B 0
Success, all matching files downloaded.
.TP
.B 1
The page could not be fetched (network error or HTTP 4xx/5xx).
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
The page was fetched, but one or more files failed to download.
.TP
.B 4
No usable Chrome-family browser found for \fB\-s\fR (not on \fBPATH\fR, or the \fB\-c\fR path is not an executable file).
.TP
.B 5
\fB\-s\fR was given, but Selenium is not installed (or is missing one of its own dependencies).
.TP
.B 254
Any other unexpected error (e.g. failure writing the \fB\-os\fR/\fB\-oh\fR output files).

[NOTES]
Selenium mode (\fB\-s\fR) works best with Selenium 4.18 or newer. With an
older Selenium, such as the python3-selenium package on some older
distribution releases, zipgetter prints a warning to standard error and
carries on, but rendering may fail or misbehave with current browsers and
chromedriver. No warning is printed without \fB\-s\fR.

[SEE ALSO]
https://github.com/JCCyC/zipgetter
